WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
AI Cloud Lab uses robots and models to compress protein engineering from years to days. This is Planetarian Daily, Episode 232. Childhood measles after immunization gaps, carbon from human metabolism, and peanuts and brain insulin follow. Then Spotlight. McCormick Professor Julius Lux leads the Dream Cloud Lab at Northwestern after the National Science Foundation awarded the Center for Synthetic Biology $20 million over four years. The Daily Northwestern describes a

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:34.180
facility that pairs computing hardware with robots that carry out much of the synthesis

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.020
in cell-free lysate on plates.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.960
Models trained on large data sets take over much of the guessing that used to dominate

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:42.320
protein sequence testing.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.700
Co-principal investigator Michael Jewett at Stanford notes that the order of amino acids

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.940
sets a protein's shape, and that shape decides whether it works as an antibody, a detergent,

00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:54.740
or a detector of contaminants.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:01:00.400
The dream-brain chatbot will let remote users specify desired protein parameters and receive

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.120
a data package after synthesis and characterization.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:09.940
Four initial science drivers focus on metal recovery, plastic degradation, biosensing, and

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.320
protein-based materials.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:17.180
Lux assembled a partnership between Northwestern scientists, Stanford University, and the Chicago

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.720
Biomedical Consortium.

00:01:19.648 --> 00:01:24.988
Childhood measles climbed again after pandemic disruptions to routine immunization, according

00:01:24.988 --> 00:01:31.548
to a global study in nature medicine. The GBD-2023 measles collaborators tracked both infections

00:01:31.548 --> 00:01:36.248
and mortality across regions where routine immunization schedules had been interrupted.

00:01:36.828 --> 00:01:43.788
Nearly 16 million children under age 5 contracted measles in 2023, with 118,000 deaths.

00:01:44.448 --> 00:01:48.248
Vaccination rates fell after public health programs and funding were disrupted,

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:53.408
reversing a decades-long decline. The compilation drew on surveillance systems that

00:01:53.408 --> 00:01:57.668
captured confirmed cases and modeled estimates for areas with incomplete reporting.

00:01:58.388 --> 00:02:02.228
Authors noted that the reversal affected the previous trajectory of steady reductions

00:02:02.228 --> 00:02:03.928
achieved over prior decades.

00:02:04.939 --> 00:02:12.079
A University of Bath led analysis of 216,502 people estimated bodily carbon dioxide output

00:02:12.079 --> 00:02:15.139
across three decades, according to Fizz.org.

00:02:15.759 --> 00:02:19.139
Annual output reached 2.05 billion metric tons.

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:23.759
That figure was 74% higher in 2015 than in 1985.

00:02:24.539 --> 00:02:29.759
Investigators calculated individual metabolic rates from demographic and dietary data before

00:02:29.759 --> 00:02:32.099
scaling to national and global populations.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:37.319
The rise reflects both population growth and shifts in average body mass and activity

00:02:37.319 --> 00:02:38.659
patterns over that span.

00:02:39.399 --> 00:02:44.659
The resulting quantity is a measurable flux within the terrestrial carbon cycle that had previously

00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:46.559
received limited quantification.

00:02:46.559 --> 00:02:52.697
Older adults who ate unsalted skin-roasted peanuts daily showed stronger insulin signaling

00:02:52.697 --> 00:02:54.557
in memory-related brain regions.

00:02:55.037 --> 00:02:59.857
Science Daily reported that participants received two servings each day for 16 weeks.

00:03:00.517 --> 00:03:04.717
Imaging and metabolic assessments before and after the period showed measurable shifts

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.457
in regional insulin signaling.

00:03:06.997 --> 00:03:11.517
The peanuts were a single addition to usual diets, with no other prescribed changes.

00:03:12.037 --> 00:03:16.677
The work focused on brain regions where age-related insulin resistance has been associated

00:03:16.677 --> 00:03:22.317
with later cognitive decline. That insulin responsiveness typically declines with age and links

00:03:22.317 --> 00:03:28.159
to Alzheimer's risk. Remote users of dream can receive the physical protein itself after

00:03:28.159 --> 00:03:33.299
the robot's finished characterization. The interface interprets a natural language request,

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:38.639
then robotic liquid handlers assemble DNA constructs in self-free lysate reactions

00:03:38.639 --> 00:03:44.979
and run functional assays. Senior personnel Ashley Kareem explained that proteins will be assembled

00:03:44.979 --> 00:03:50.039
reproducibly at small volumes, so robots can pipette and move trays through measurement

00:03:50.039 --> 00:03:55.979
and analysis steps. Executive Director Michelle Hoffman of the Chicago Biomedical Consortium

00:03:55.979 --> 00:04:01.479
described the chatbot as accepting natural language requests and then returning job status

00:04:01.479 --> 00:04:07.299
updates plus final data packages. Hoffman noted that after the initial prompt, the chatbot will

00:04:07.299 --> 00:04:13.059
present menus of parameters, guiding non-specialists through feasible design choices before synthesis

00:04:13.059 --> 00:04:13.679
basis begins.

00:04:14.339 --> 00:04:19.259
The bio-foundry already owned by the Center for Synthetic Biology will be augmented with

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:23.479
new computational infrastructure, robotic liquid handlers, and staffing.

00:04:24.319 --> 00:04:29.019
Careem highlighted reproducible small-volume reactions that robots can handle consistently

00:04:29.019 --> 00:04:30.619
across thousands of variants.

00:04:31.662 --> 00:04:36.482
Most people assume a new protein still has to be built by testing amino acid strings one

00:04:36.482 --> 00:04:38.442
at a time over years of bench work.

00:04:38.442 --> 00:04:44.322
Models can predict folding patterns and functional properties from sequence data alone, then pass

00:04:44.322 --> 00:04:46.722
the strongest candidates to automated assembly.

00:04:47.362 --> 00:04:52.582
Machine learning algorithms identify statistical patterns that link sequence to shape and activity

00:04:52.582 --> 00:04:55.202
from large collections of known protein structures.

00:04:55.842 --> 00:04:59.682
The model then proposes variants likely to perform a requested task.

00:05:00.342 --> 00:05:04.822
Plate readers record whether the resulting proteins bind their targets or catalyze the

00:05:04.822 --> 00:05:05.722
desired reaction.

00:05:05.722 --> 00:05:11.442
Antibodies that recognize pathogens and enzymes that process nutrients are already doing

00:05:11.442 --> 00:05:12.842
this work inside the body.

00:05:13.462 --> 00:05:18.462
New versions of those molecules are created for medicines, industrial cleaners, and environmental

00:05:18.462 --> 00:05:19.142
sensors.

00:05:19.782 --> 00:05:24.802
The AI handles the initial exploration of sequence space while the hardware carries out construction

00:05:24.802 --> 00:05:25.442
and testing.

00:05:25.942 --> 00:05:33.802
In October 2025, 135 letters of interest arrive from AI companies, research groups, and academic

00:05:33.802 --> 00:05:39.402
institutions across 48 states within 48 hours. Centralizing the bio-foundry

00:05:39.402 --> 00:05:42.902
and the computing stack removes the requirement that every research team

00:05:42.902 --> 00:05:48.075
maintain its own expensive automation suite. Lux emphasized that the goal is

00:05:48.075 --> 00:05:52.255
to solve the protein engineering bottleneck once, so multiple downstream

00:05:52.255 --> 00:05:56.295
biotechnology applications can proceed without repeating the same manual

00:05:56.295 --> 00:06:01.295
optimization work. One open question is how broadly the models will generalize

00:06:01.295 --> 00:06:06.907
once they move past the first validation cases. Performance data from those cases will show

00:06:06.907 --> 00:06:11.567
whether the predictions hold across diverse functional requirements and whether assembly

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:16.927
stays consistent at the scale needed for broader adoption. The first drivers were chosen to

00:06:16.927 --> 00:06:22.127
represent common protein engineering goals, a practical test of whether the end-to-end pipeline

00:06:22.127 --> 00:06:28.087
delivers usable molecules rather than only faster calculations. The lab aims to serve as a

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:32.867
midwest engine for biotechnology and to ease a bottleneck many developers still face.

00:06:33.905 --> 00:06:39.085
UCLA investigators linked long-term exposure to one widely used pesticide with more than

00:06:39.085 --> 00:06:42.065
2.5 times higher Parkinson's disease risk.

00:06:42.605 --> 00:06:47.425
The work combined epidemiological records with cellular assays to map both the elevated

00:06:47.425 --> 00:06:50.325
disease odds and the intracellular damage mechanism.

00:06:51.365 --> 00:06:55.685
Investigators traced how the chemical harms brain cells and identified a potential protective

00:06:55.685 --> 00:06:55.985
root.

00:06:55.985 --> 00:07:00.925
They also tested interventions that preserve cell viability despite the exposure.

00:07:01.365 --> 00:07:05.865
The findings add a specific environmental factor to the set of known contributors to

00:07:05.865 --> 00:07:07.005
Parkinson's incidents.

00:07:07.939 --> 00:07:12.699
Crown of thorns starfish on Australia's Great Barrier Reef often fed without destroying

00:07:12.699 --> 00:07:13.539
whole colonies.

00:07:14.159 --> 00:07:18.679
Nearly 75% of observed feeding events left living coral tissue intact.

00:07:19.379 --> 00:07:24.519
By consuming fast growing dominant corals, the predator's open space for slower growing species.

00:07:24.519 --> 00:07:29.539
disease. The observations covered multiple reef sites where starfish densities remain below

00:07:29.539 --> 00:07:34.679
outbreak thresholds. Partial feeding events allowed surviving coral fragments to recover

00:07:34.679 --> 00:07:39.836
and permitted recruitment of additional species. Habitual T-consumption was tracked

00:07:39.836 --> 00:07:43.256
against heart and blood vessel disease in a large adult cohort.

00:07:43.916 --> 00:07:49.536
Incidents was 11% lower among people who drank tea regularly. The cohort numbered nearly

00:07:49.536 --> 00:07:51.516
486,000 adults.

00:07:52.096 --> 00:07:57.156
Risk reached its lowest point at roughly 6 to 8 cups daily, with black tea showing

00:07:57.156 --> 00:07:58.916
steadier benefits than green tea.

00:07:59.576 --> 00:08:04.556
Data collection captured self-reported intake frequency alongside verified medical outcomes

00:08:04.556 --> 00:08:06.516
over an extended follow-up period.

00:08:07.076 --> 00:08:12.916
The dose response curve indicated a plateau beyond the 6 to 8 cup range, and black tea held

00:08:12.916 --> 00:08:17.056
the association across subgroups while green tea benefits appeared more variable.

00:08:17.056 --> 00:08:23.067
A specimen recovered in Egypt challenges the long-standing view that East Africa was the sole

00:08:23.067 --> 00:08:24.427
cradle of ape evolution.

00:08:24.907 --> 00:08:30.727
The fossil is 17 million years old, from the early myocene, and preserves dental and skeletal

00:08:30.727 --> 00:08:32.967
features that align with later ape lineages.

00:08:33.607 --> 00:08:38.147
Researchers now suggest North Africa and the Middle East may have played earlier roles.

00:08:38.627 --> 00:08:43.747
Its location extends the geographic range previously considered for the earliest diversification

00:08:43.747 --> 00:08:44.107
events.

00:08:44.107 --> 00:08:49.927
The fine prompts re-examination of migration and speciation models that had centered exclusively

00:08:49.927 --> 00:08:51.487
on East African sites.

00:08:52.437 --> 00:08:57.517
Southern hemisphere plantings of conifers outperformed their northern hemisphere source populations,

00:08:57.937 --> 00:08:59.357
according to Fizz.org.

00:08:59.877 --> 00:09:05.697
Across 192 sites on four continents, trees grown far from their evolutionary origins

00:09:05.697 --> 00:09:08.237
put on biomass up to four times faster.

00:09:08.997 --> 00:09:12.537
Drought resistance remained intact despite that accelerated accumulation.

00:09:12.537 --> 00:09:18.717
The study aggregated long-term forestry trial data to compare performance across match genetic

00:09:18.717 --> 00:09:19.517
provenences.

00:09:19.997 --> 00:09:23.957
Faster growth arrived without increased mortality under variable rainfall.

00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:28.997
Researchers at the Radcliffe Department of Medicine developed a new approach to liver

00:09:28.997 --> 00:09:31.117
testing that avoids invasive procedures.

00:09:31.557 --> 00:09:36.837
The technique aims to provide equivalent diagnostic information through imaging or biomarker

00:09:36.837 --> 00:09:39.357
combinations that do not require tissue sampling.

00:09:39.357 --> 00:09:44.617
Early validation focused on accuracy relative to established biopsy standards.

00:09:45.037 --> 00:09:50.717
The advance addresses patient burden and procedural risks associated with conventional liver evaluation.

00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:55.157
Details of the method and validation data appear on the department site.

00:09:56.167 --> 00:10:01.927
Elsewhere, Fizz.org notes that decades of decisions on contraception, abortion care, HIV programs,

00:10:02.527 --> 00:10:07.967
and sexuality education have moved predominantly from high income to lower income regions,

00:10:07.967 --> 00:10:11.547
limiting recognition of communal knowledge in the global south.

00:10:12.027 --> 00:10:15.507
Five Canadian provinces and territories have ended clock changes,

00:10:16.087 --> 00:10:19.827
raising concern that later sunrises under permanent daylight saving time

00:10:19.827 --> 00:10:22.867
could reduce sleep for students whose schedules remained fixed.

00:10:23.607 --> 00:10:27.627
Traditional owners report declining health of culturally significant desert plants

00:10:27.627 --> 00:10:31.847
around Uluru, Katachuda as temperatures and rainfall patterns shift.

00:10:32.407 --> 00:10:35.907
Before we go, performance data from the Dream Cloud Lab will test

00:10:35.907 --> 00:10:39.447
whether the AI predictions hold across diverse functional requirements.

00:10:39.987 --> 00:10:41.967
That's Planetarian Daily for today.

